# Code Quality Rules

## File size

- Target: < 200 lines per file
- Hard limit: 800 lines — split first if you would exceed this
- Exception: generated files (lock files, build output)

## Function size

- Target: < 30 lines per function
- Hard limit: 50 lines — extract helpers first if you would exceed this

## Naming

- Variables and functions: `camelCase`, descriptive
- Types and interfaces: `PascalCase`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- Booleans: `is`, `has`, `should`, `can` prefix

## Immutability

- Never mutate function arguments
- Return new objects for updates: `{ ...original, field: newValue }`
- `const` by default; `let` only when reassignment is genuinely needed

## Abstractions

- Do not introduce abstractions for fewer than 3 real use cases
- Duplication is preferable to the wrong abstraction
- Refactor in a separate commit, not mixed with feature work

## Before marking done

- [ ] No `console.log` or debug statements
- [ ] No unused variables or imports
- [ ] Types explicit on all exported functions
- [ ] No `any` in new code
